The correlation between closeted homosexuality and internalized homophobia exists because being in the closet often requires individuals to hide their true selves and adopt socially acceptable behaviors and beliefs that contradict their own feelings and experiences. This constant denial and repression of one's sexuality can lead to negative self-perceptions and a fear of being discovered or rejected by others.

